# One month of Claude Max with Opus 5.5 later

I value engineering. I like good quality code, I like reading code, and I like knowing why something works the way it does. So it feels a bit odd to write this post: over one month of Claude Max with Opus 5.5 I semi-vibe-coded, and partly fully vibe-coded, nine Android apps, a few Linux and server counterparts, a personal F-Droid repository to ship them all, and a whole video game. It showed me that the way software gets made has changed. For personal apps like these, it's absolutely worth it.

This post tells the story of that month: the F-Droid repository, every app in it, the servers behind them, and why I cancelled the subscription at the end.

=> ./one-month-of-claude-max/hero.jpg Some of the apps: TurboNotes, Player, TurboMon, TurboLaunch, File Browser and RESTForge

